  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Algebraically, find the set of values $x$ such that:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(x+2)(x-1)\\ge 0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\le -2$ or $x\\ge 1$.",
          "worked": "Both factors must be non-negative or both non-positive.\n\nCase 1: $x+2\\ge0$ and $x-1\\ge0$, giving $x\\ge1$.\n\nCase 2: $x+2\\le0$ and $x-1\\le0$, giving $x\\le-2$.\n\nTherefore, $x\\le-2$ or $x\\ge1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(x-3)(x-2)<0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2<x<3$.",
          "worked": "The factors must have opposite signs.\n\nCase 1: $x-3<0$ and $x-2>0$, giving $2<x<3$.\n\nCase 2: $x-3>0$ and $x-2<0$ would require $x>3$ and $x<2$, which is impossible.\n\nTherefore, $2<x<3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$x^2+5x+6\\le0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-3\\le x\\le-2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+5x+6&\\le0\\\\(x+2)(x+3)&\\le0\\end{align*}$$\nThe factors must have opposite signs, or at least one must be zero.\n\nCase 1: $x+2\\le0$ and $x+3\\ge0$, giving $-3\\le x\\le-2$.\n\nCase 2: $x+2\\ge0$ and $x+3\\le0$ would require $x\\ge-2$ and $x\\le-3$, which is impossible.\n\nTherefore, $-3\\le x\\le-2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$x^2-6x+8>0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<2$ or $x>4$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-6x+8&>0\\\\(x-2)(x-4)&>0\\end{align*}$$\nBoth factors must be positive or both negative.\n\nCase 1: $x-2>0$ and $x-4>0$, giving $x>4$.\n\nCase 2: $x-2<0$ and $x-4<0$, giving $x<2$.\n\nTherefore, $x<2$ or $x>4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
